# The OS server's stacks (roadmap os-server.md P5): each of its threads has
# 1 KB of its data segment, filled at its first start; the shell's thread,
# after the deepest calls the shell makes - a directory of two clusters, a
# file through the FAT, a cd, ps, a fault reported - has a quarter of its
# part or more to spare when the shell exits (TEST_OS_STACKS).
program: shell
define: TEST_OS_STACKS
keys: dir b:\\many\ntype c:\\docs\\hello.txt\ncd c:\\docs\nps\ncrash gp\nexit\n
match: contains
timeout: 120
emulators: bochs mame
---
rx286 shell, started again
os: a thread's stack: a quarter of it or more to spare: yes
